@meta
id: 14-08
title: Drill — from here down
chapter: 14
type: drill
skills: sub-range
par: 30
minutes: 4
reps: 8
vscode: find the marker, shift-click the last line, Ctrl-H in selection
open: queues.ts

@brief
Eight times: everything below the `// v2 consumers` marker is on v2
now and still says `v1`. The retired v1 block above the marker keeps
its names.

Search to the marker, substitute from there to the end, save.

@keys
| `/text` `Enter` | put the cursor on the marker line |
| `:.,$s/old/new/` `Enter` | from the cursor line to the end of the file |

@hints
The search is the range's starting point. Land on the marker and the
rest is `.,$`.
--
`/v2 con` `Enter`, then `:.,$s/v1/v2/` and Enter.

@solution
    /v2 con<Enter>  :.,$s/v1/v2/<Enter>  :wq<Enter>

Twenty-five keystrokes, and `v1` in the retired block is never at risk
because the range does not reach it. By the last rep the search and
the range should feel like one movement: aim, then sweep downward.

@start queues.ts
// v1 consumers, retired on 1 October
export const ORDER_CREATED = 'orders.created.v1';
export const ORDER_PAID = 'orders.paid.v1';
export const ORDER_SHIPPED = 'orders.shipped.v1';

// v2 consumers
export const REFUND_CREATED = 'refunds.created.v1';
export const REFUND_APPROVED = 'refunds.approved.v1';
export const REFUND_REJECTED = 'refunds.rejected.v1';
export const REFUND_SETTLED = 'refunds.settled.v1';

@expected queues.ts
// v1 consumers, retired on 1 October
export const ORDER_CREATED = 'orders.created.v1';
export const ORDER_PAID = 'orders.paid.v1';
export const ORDER_SHIPPED = 'orders.shipped.v1';

// v2 consumers
export const REFUND_CREATED = 'refunds.created.v2';
export const REFUND_APPROVED = 'refunds.approved.v2';
export const REFUND_REJECTED = 'refunds.rejected.v2';
export const REFUND_SETTLED = 'refunds.settled.v2';
